# Wheel of Fortune makes both players discard their hands in one move. Bot2's Darksteel Colossus is revealed and shuffled
# into Bot2's library (CR 701.24a); Bot1 puts its Lightning Bolt and Island on top of its own library with Library of Leng.
# Only Bot2's library was shuffled, so Bot1 still arranges the two cards on top of Bot1's (CR 401.4) - the shuffle of
# another library takes no position from them. The shuffles are fixed to reverse ([Shuffles]): Bot2's seven draws are the
# Plains that were at the bottom of its library, and Bot1's are the Bolt and the Island and five Forests from the top.
[Shuffles]
Reverse

[Bot1 Deck]
Library of Leng
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Wheel of Fortune
Lightning Bolt
Island
Plains
Forest x10
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Darksteel Colossus
Island x6
Island x10
Plains x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Library of Leng.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Wheel of Fortune.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Arrange(Lightning Bolt; Island)
[T1 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Shuffles = 0
Bot2.Shuffles = 1
Bot1.Hand = Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest; Island; Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Graveyard = Wheel of Fortune; Plains; Black Lotus
Bot2.Hand = Plains; Plains; Plains; Plains; Plains; Plains; Plains
Bot2.Library.Count = 14
